# Saved run fixtures policy

`inference-resolver/backend/app/data/fixtures/*.json` are **saved, realistic run
results** for the demo case studies (`cern`, `covid`, `eggs`). The UI loads them
when a case-study chip is clicked so the app can be tested with zero LLM calls.
Each fixture contains the full run result plus every raw LLM exchange
(`call_details`), all produced by real pipeline runs.

## Required behavior

1. **Regenerate on format change.** Whenever the run-result data format changes —
   `RunResult` / `Claim` / `Link` / `CallSummary` / `StageSummary` in
   `backend/app/models.py`, the artifact schema in `backend/app/main.py`, or the
   fixture shape itself — regenerate all fixtures with realistic data:
   start the backend with a valid `XAI_API_KEY`, then run
   `python scripts/generate_fixtures.py` from `inference-resolver/backend/`.
2. **Fixtures must stay realistic.** Never hand-edit fixtures into shapes the
   live pipeline cannot produce. They are faithful captured outputs, not mocks.
3. **If regeneration is impossible** (e.g. no API key available), mechanically
   migrate the fixtures to the new schema so the UI keeps working, and tell the
   user they should be regenerated with live runs.
4. **New demos need fixtures.** When a demo is added to
   `backend/app/data/demos.json`, generate its fixture in the same way.
